1. An organic light-emitting component comprising:

a first electrode;

an organic emission layer stack arranged over the first electrode;

a second electrode arranged over the organic emission layer stack, the first electrode and the second electrode being configured to inject charge carriers into the organic emission layer stack for generation of light; and

a current spreading structure electrically coupled to at least one of the first electrode and the second electrode, the current spreading structure comprising a metal structure configured to laterally distribute current across an active area of the organic light-emitting component,

wherein at least a portion of the metal structure is provided with a passivation layer comprising a semiconductor chalcogenide, the passivation layer being arranged to inhibit interaction between the metal structure and material of the organic light-emitting component while permitting electrical operation of the organic light-emitting component.
